From: Redmi AX3000 NSS integration
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: release NSS and stop CE before the reset power cycle

ath11k_core_reset() power-cycled the userpd while NSS still owned the
SoC rings; NSS teardown ran only later, in reconfigure_on_crash() after
the new firmware reported ready. Masking host IRQs does not stop the NSS
core. On opt66 a hw-restart of b00a040.wifi rebooted pd-2 and 0.47 s later
its IST raised NOC_error.c:359, the Q6 root PD failed to restart (-110)
and both radios stayed down until a full reboot.

Tear down this SoC's NSS wifili instance after the radios park in
op_start (which waits without conf_mutex) and before power down, and clear
nss.enabled so the later teardown is a no-op and the existing reconfigure
path re-enables and rebuilds NSS. If teardown fails, ring ownership is
uncertain: keep the target powered, finish the reset bookkeeping and stop
automatic retries instead of risking the shared root PD.

With only that change, sta53dbg no longer hit the NOC and 2.4 GHz stayed
up, but QCN6122 recovery failed with "Service connect timeout". The raw
ce_irq_disable op masks CE IRQs without clearing CE_IRQ_ENABLED, so
ath11k_pcic_start() skipped re-enabling them; HTC wait_target recovered by
polling, the HTT service connect does not poll. Stop CE through hif_stop(),
whose state hif_start() restores on both the AHB and the pcic ops.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2664,7 +2664,7 @@
 static void ath11k_core_reset(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct ath11k_base *ab = container_of(work, struct ath11k_base, reset_work);
-	int reset_count, fail_cont_count;
+	int reset_count, fail_cont_count, ret;
 	long time_left;
 
 	if (!(test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags))) {
@@ -2727,7 +2727,32 @@
 						ATH11K_RECOVER_START_TIMEOUT_HZ);
 
 	ath11k_hif_irq_disable(ab);
-	ath11k_hif_ce_irq_disable(ab);
+	/* hif_start() re-enables only what hif_stop() recorded as disabled. The
+	 * raw ce_irq_disable op left QCN6122 CE IRQs masked after recovery, so
+	 * the HTT service connect never saw the firmware's reply.
+	 */
+	ath11k_hif_stop(ab);
+
+	/* NSS still owns this SoC's rings on its own core, and IRQ masking does
+	 * not stop it. Release that ownership before the target loses power:
+	 * a userpd rebooted under live NSS ownership raised a NOC error that
+	 * took down the shared Q6 root PD and every radio on it.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&ab->core_lock);
+	ret = ath11k_nss_teardown(ab);
+	if (!ret)
+		ab->nss.enabled = false;
+	mutex_unlock(&ab->core_lock);
+	if (ret) {
+		ath11k_err(ab, "NSS reset failed before power down: %d; keeping target powered\n",
+			   ret);
+		atomic_set(&ab->fail_cont_count, ATH11K_RESET_MAX_FAIL_COUNT_FINAL);
+		ab->is_reset = false;
+		atomic_dec(&ab->reset_count);
+		complete(&ab->reset_complete);
+		return;
+	}
+	ath11k_info(ab, "NSS released before reset power cycle\n");
 
 	ath11k_hif_power_down(ab, false);
 	ath11k_hif_power_up(ab);
